><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>(1) Elite race walkers readily experience rectal temperatures&#xD;&gt;40°C during competition in warm environmental conditions,&#xD;without coinciding signs and symptoms of heat illness&#xD;(ie, central nervous system dysfunction).&#xD;(2) It is possible for a range of cooling strategies to be implemented&#xD;on elite athletes in major championship events&#xD;including cold-water immersion, ice-slurry ingestion, icedtowel&#xD;application, ice-jacket application, and facial water&#xD;spraying.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
